From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ep9
Subject: [PATCH] icu_calendar: the published 2.3.0 manifest, so a checkout
 builds on its own

The icu4x workspace gives components/calendar its dependencies through
`workspace = true` and path entries, so a [patch.crates-io] path to
this directory from another workspace would build icu_provider,
icu_locale_core, tinystr, zerovec and the other ICU4X crates from this
checkout, not the crates.io packages that the rest of the graph uses
(two copies of each, and two sets of types).

This replaces components/calendar/Cargo.toml with the manifest of the
crates.io icu_calendar 2.3.0 package (the file that `cargo package`
wrote; its sources equal src/ at this commit), which names each
dependency by its crates.io version and inherits nothing.

Not for upstream: only a downstream [patch] needs it.
